Description: VeltOS Disk Management, Windows 11's Disk Management layout
 The volume list over the disk map, as Windows' Disk Management shows
 them: every disk ("Disk 0", "CD-ROM 0") with its partitions and
 unallocated space to scale. Format a volume, delete it, make a new
 simple volume in unallocated space, change its label, mount, unmount and
 eject, or initialize a blank disk (GPT or MBR). Everything goes through
 UDisks2 (busctl), which asks for the administrator's password where
 needed and keeps the running system's volumes safe.
